"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#2-set-the-initial-theme","content":"2\\. Set the initial theme"},"1276":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#3-add-a-theme-toggle","content":"3\\. Add a theme toggle"},"1277":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#1-install-tailwind-css","content":"Create an Astro project and set it up with Tailwind CSS. If Tailwind CSS hasn't been set up yet, follow the official installation guide."},"1278":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#2-install-the-react-integration","content":"Hummingbird React components need Astro's React integration."},"1279":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#3-install-hummingbird-react","content":"Install Hummingbird React via a preferred package manager."},"1280":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#4-import-css","content":"Import Hummingbird styles in the main CSS file. The package registers its own Tailwind `@source` paths, so no additional configuration is needed."},"1281":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#5-use-components","content":"Import any component and use it in `.astro` pages or React islands. Static components render without a client directive; interactive components (dropdowns, modals, tooltips, etc.) need one, such as `client:load`."},"1282":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#dark-mode","content":"Hummingbird uses class-based dark mode - a `.dark` class on `<html>` switches the whole theme. See Dark Mode for details and customization."},"1283":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#1-add-the-dark-variant","content":"Register the class-based dark variant after the style imports."},"1284":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#2-set-the-initial-theme","content":"Apply the saved theme with an inline script in the layout `<head>` - it runs before first paint, so there is no flash of the wrong theme. `is:inline` keeps Astro from bundling and deferring it."},"1285":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/astro#3-add-a-theme-toggle","content":"Add `DarkThemeToggle` to your page. It needs a client directive to be interactive. `DarkThemeToggle` switches between light and dark mode, persists the choice, and keeps browser tabs in sync. For custom controls, use the `useThemeMode` hook."},"1286":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/gatsby","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/framework-guides/gatsby","type":"page","content":"Gatsby"